563
00:54:47,070 --> 00:54:49,590
The next thing that you can do is go to a larger.
你可以做的下一件事是采用更大的。

564
00:54:49,590 --> 00:54:51,650
But you already saw how expensive that is.
但你已经看到了，这有多昂贵。

565
00:54:51,650 --> 00:54:54,830
And then you have the third factor, the K1.
然后你还有第三个因素，即 K1。

566
00:54:54,830 --> 00:55:00,850
And I kind of feel a little bit pretentious being here,
我觉得有点自命不凡，居然能站在这里，

567
00:55:00,850 --> 00:55:09,110
because then we start talking about computational lithography and who am I daring to show up here at Berkeley, where
因为接下来我们就要讨论计算光刻，而我算哪根葱，竟敢出现在伯克利，这里

568
00:55:09,110 --> 00:55:15,210
one of your professors, Andy neureuter he's really the godfather of computational lithography.
你们的一位教授安迪·诺伊特勒，他才是计算光刻的奠基人。

569
00:55:15,210 --> 00:55:18,750
So I'm basically preaching to the choir.
所以我基本上是在对懂行的人讲话。

570
00:55:18,750 --> 00:55:23,310
But allow me anyway to share my view on some of this.
但请允许我仍然分享一下我的看法。

571
00:55:23,310 --> 00:55:34,750
Obviously, we stand on the shoulders of many Giants that have helped with developing a lot of the theory all the way from Fresnel, Fourier, Maxwell, Helmholtz, Ernst
显然，我们站在许多巨人的肩膀上，他们为发展大量理论做出了贡献，从菲涅尔、傅里叶、麦克斯韦、赫尔姆霍兹、恩斯特

572
00:55:34,750 --> 00:55:46,190
Abbe there, this guy here that was one of the first chief scientists of Zeiss, did a lot of work on microscopy and developed it from there.
阿贝，这位蔡司的早期首席科学家之一，他在显微镜领域做了大量工作，并由此推动了该领域的发展。

573
00:55:49,130 --> 00:55:49,950
What did he say.
他说了什么？

574
00:55:49,950 --> 00:55:52,870
He say in 1873 already.
早在1873年他就说过。

575
00:55:52,870 --> 00:56:02,010
Hey, the minimum pitch is 1/2 times the wavelength divided by the sine of that opening angle that we now call the.
嗨，最小间距等于波长的一半，除以那个我们如今称为数值孔径的开口角的正弦值。

576
00:56:02,010 --> 00:56:04,590
And he didn't have the refractive index yet.
而那时他还没有折射率的概念。

577
00:56:04,590 --> 00:56:09,530
Now we say that n times the sine of that angle is the numerical aperture.
现在我们说，n乘以该角度的正弦值就是数值孔径。

578
00:56:09,530 --> 00:56:12,810
But isn't it remarkable.
但难道不令人惊叹吗？

579
00:56:12,810 --> 00:56:25,530
Since 1873 to the day of today, a very simple formula has governed our roadmap, and the rest was simply technology.
从1873年到今天，一个非常简单的公式一直指导着我们的技术路线图，其余的都只是技术问题。

580
00:56:25,530 --> 00:56:28,890
Well, technology is not always simple.
但技术并不总是简单的。

581
00:56:28,890 --> 00:56:37,690
Lin from TSMC said, hey, lambda and Na, that's physics and that's geometry of your lenses.
台积电的林先生说，嘿，波长λ和数值孔径Na，这都是光学和镜头的几何特性。

582
00:56:37,690 --> 00:56:45,280
But that K1, that's all kind of illumination tricks chemistry, resist contrast, aberrations, and mask tricks.
但那个k1值，涉及各种照明技巧、化学工艺、光刻胶对比度、像差以及掩模技巧。

583
00:56:45,280 --> 00:56:49,320
And the minimum value that you can accomplish is 0.25.
你能达到的最小值是0.25。

584
00:56:49,320 --> 00:56:57,200
So I'm going to talk about what can we all do to reduce that K1 if we want to do that with computation.
所以我将谈谈我们能做些什么来通过计算手段降低这个k1值。

585
00:56:57,200 --> 00:57:01,220
It starts with I need to have a good model for what am I actually getting.
这始于我需要一个良好的模型，来准确反映我实际获得的结果。

586
00:57:01,220 --> 00:57:12,960
So I need a forward model with which I can predict what is the quality of the imaging that I get and that good model that will involve a MAST model.
我需要一个前向模型，能够预测我所获得的成像质量，而这个优质模型将涉及一个MAST模型。

587
00:57:12,960 --> 00:57:16,440
I need to see what is happening in my optics.
我需要观察光学系统中发生了什么。

588
00:57:16,440 --> 00:57:18,620
What is the reaction of my resist.
我需要了解光刻胶的反应情况。

589
00:57:18,620 --> 00:57:20,040
That's a lot of chemistry.
这涉及大量的化学知识。

590
00:57:20,040 --> 00:57:23,340
And ultimately, I don't care what the pattern is, am I resist.
最终，我不在乎这个模式是什么，我就是抗拒。

591
00:57:23,340 --> 00:57:25,740
I want it to have it in a device layer.
我希望它能存在于器件层中。

592
00:57:25,740 --> 00:57:30,080
So I need an edge model that becomes my forward model.
因此我需要一个边缘模型，作为我的前向模型。

593
00:57:30,080 --> 00:57:36,840
And a lot of effort has gone into how do I make that forward model as good as I can.
为此投入了大量努力，以使这个前向模型尽可能完善。

594
00:57:36,840 --> 00:57:39,220
And we continue to improve with that.
我们仍在持续改进。

595
00:57:39,220 --> 00:57:41,760
More and more physics, more and more chemistry.
越来越多的物理，越来越多的化学。

596
00:57:41,760 --> 00:57:45,760
And at some point in time, we said, hey, AI is starting to take off.
某个时刻，我们意识到，AI 开始兴起。

597
00:57:45,760 --> 00:57:48,340
And perhaps when we have a lot of good measurements,
或许当我们拥有大量优质测量数据时，

598
00:57:48,340 --> 00:57:59,580
we can develop an AI model that can predict what I will get, even without fully understanding why that is what I will get and all of that is being employed.
我们可以开发出一个AI模型，预测我将得到的结果，即使尚未完全理解其背后的原因，而这一切正在被应用。

599
00:57:59,580 --> 00:58:04,180
But once I have such a good model, I can go and play all kinds of tricks.
但一旦我拥有了这样一个出色的模型，我就能施展各种手段。

600
00:58:04,180 --> 00:58:13,880
I can make a little manufacturing check where with a little layer and a little model that I have developed, I can now say, what am I going to get on the wafer.
我可以进行一次小小的制造检查，仅凭一个薄层和我开发出的一个模型，现在就能预测我在晶圆上将得到什么。

601
00:58:13,880 --> 00:58:17,620
And is that what I wanted in the first place.
那正是我最初想要的东西吗。

602
00:58:17,620 --> 00:58:23,600
Another option is that I say, hey, I have a little layer and I have measurements on what is the wafer.
另一种选择是，我说，嘿，我有一个小层，我有晶圆上的测量数据。

603
00:58:23,600 --> 00:58:28,860
I can calibrate that model or I have a little model.
我可以校准这个模型，或者我有一个小模型。

604
00:58:28,860 --> 00:58:31,220
I know what I want on the wafer.
我知道我想要在晶圆上实现什么。

605
00:58:31,220 --> 00:58:37,180
What do I need to put on my reticle so that I get, in the end, what I wanted in the first place.
我需要在掩模上放置什么，才能最终得到我最初想要的结果。

606
00:58:37,180 --> 00:58:40,070
And you contributed quite a bit of that.
你在其中贡献了不少。

607
00:58:40,070 --> 00:58:43,110
That's where the field of inverse lithography and so on.
这就是逆光刻等领域所在。

608
00:58:43,110 --> 00:58:45,230
I'm going to talk about a different one today.
今天我要讲的是另一个不同的方向。

609
00:58:45,230 --> 00:58:46,650
And that's this one here.
就是这个。

610
00:58:46,650 --> 00:58:48,510
I know what I want on the wafer.
我知道我想要在晶圆上实现什么。

611
00:58:48,510 --> 00:58:50,030
How can I optimize.
我该如何优化。

612
00:58:50,030 --> 00:58:52,730
What is the pattern that I put on the little layer.
我在小层上放置的图案应该是什么。

613
00:58:52,730 --> 00:58:56,070
And how do I instruct my scanner.
我该如何指导我的扫描仪。

614
00:58:56,070 --> 00:59:04,850
What is the illumination that I will use on the scanner to maximize the contrast to get the best possible results.
我应该使用怎样的照明，才能最大化对比度，获得最佳结果。

615
00:59:04,850 --> 00:59:11,450
Now, when we talk about illumination, let me talk for a moment about an illumination system.
当我们谈到照明时，让我先简单介绍一下照明系统。

616
00:59:11,450 --> 00:59:18,530
Trick is what I would like to have is very, very uniform illumination of my mask.
我希望我的掩模获得非常非常均匀的照明。

617
00:59:18,530 --> 00:59:28,330
And in order to play with interference and to play with diffraction and be able to manipulate exactly what is the interference pattern
为了操控干涉和衍射，并精确控制在晶圆上形成的干涉图样，

618
00:59:28,330 --> 00:59:35,610
that I get on the wafer, I need to make sure that this is spatially coherent light.
我必须确保这是空间相干光。

619
00:59:35,610 --> 00:59:37,150
And how do we do that.
我们是如何做到这一点的？

620
00:59:37,150 --> 00:59:40,190
We create this so-called 4f system.
我们构建了所谓的4f系统。

621
00:59:40,190 --> 00:59:45,990
A guy Kohler invented this by having this four lens system.
科勒先生通过这种四透镜系统发明了它。

622
00:59:45,990 --> 00:59:55,230
What I can create is, for every point in the light source, there is one particular set of planar waves that hits the mask.
对于光源中的每一个点，都会有一组特定的平面波照射到掩模上。

623
00:59:55,230 --> 01:00:04,550
So if I imagine myself sitting on the mask and I look back at the illumination, imagine a circle
如果我想象自己坐在掩模上，回头看向照明系统，想象一个圆形，

624
01:00:04,550 --> 01:00:07,570
and I could get light from that whole circle at me.
我就能从整个圆周接收到光线。

625
01:00:07,570 --> 01:00:09,750
That would be a cone of light.
那将是一束光锥。

626
01:00:09,750 --> 01:00:13,250
I could have light just coming from the center of that point.
我可以让光仅从该点中心射出。

627
01:00:13,250 --> 01:00:15,710
That would be one planar wave.
那将是一束平面波。

628
01:00:15,710 --> 01:00:22,330
I will also show you that I can have light coming from there and from there, and then I get very particular diffraction.
我还将向你们展示，我可以让光从那里和那里射出，从而产生非常特定的衍射。

629
01:00:22,330 --> 01:00:25,250
And that's all the optimization that we're going to do.
这就是我们所要进行的所有优化。

630
01:00:28,270 --> 01:00:35,780
So here you see that a little bit for every point in my source plane in the illumination I now get a number.
所以在这里，你看到对于光源平面中的每一个点，照明中现在都会对应一个数值。

631
01:00:35,780 --> 01:00:41,820
I got plane waves onto the mask that leads to diffraction.
我将平面波投射到掩模上，从而产生衍射。

632
01:00:41,820 --> 01:00:45,040
So the diffraction orders are captured by the objective lens.
衍射级次由物镜镜头捕捉。

633
01:00:45,040 --> 01:00:48,400
And the bigger this lens, the bigger these opening angles,
镜头越大，这些开口角度就越大，

634
01:00:48,400 --> 01:00:56,000
the more of these diffraction patterns I capture, and the better will be the reconstruction of the image here on the image plane.
我就能捕捉到越多的衍射图案，从而在像平面上的图像重建效果就越好。

635
01:00:56,000 --> 01:00:58,980
That's basically Fourier optics.
这基本上就是傅里叶光学。

636
01:00:58,980 --> 01:01:09,420
So let's look a little bit more at diffraction for those of you that are not totally familiar with that, Mr. Huygens already said, hey, when you have light hitting an opening,
所以让我们再深入一点看看衍射，对于那些不太熟悉这个概念的观众，惠更斯先生早就说过，当光照射到一个开口上时，

637
01:01:09,420 --> 01:01:14,900
each point here starts to act as a source of spherical waves,
这里的每个点开始表现为球面波的源，

638
01:01:14,900 --> 01:01:26,000
and it's really the path optical path length differences that then create this pattern here, where in some directions I end up getting light, and in other directions I do not get light.
真正造成这种图案的是光程差，导致某些方向上有光，而其他方向上没有光。

639
01:01:26,000 --> 01:01:28,900
And those are called the diffraction orders.
这些被称为衍射级次。

640
01:01:28,900 --> 01:01:37,440
In essence, if I look at my aperture, the mask, and I think of that as a repeating pattern.
本质上，如果我观察我的数值孔径、掩模，并将其视为一个重复的图案。

641
01:01:37,440 --> 01:01:44,880
I can take the Fourier transform of that pattern, and every diffraction order encodes one of the Fourier components.
我可以对这个图案进行傅里叶变换，每个衍射级次都编码了傅里叶分量之一。

642
01:01:44,880 --> 01:01:47,640
And you can think of the lens as a filter.
你可以把镜头看作是一种滤镜。

643
01:01:47,640 --> 01:01:51,700
How many of the Fourier components can I capture that lead.
我能捕捉到多少个傅里叶分量，从而实现领先？

644
01:01:51,700 --> 01:01:54,660
Help me reconstruct the pattern of the mask.
帮我重建掩模的图案。

645
01:01:54,660 --> 01:01:58,120
Now on the wafer.
现在在晶圆上。

646
01:01:58,120 --> 01:02:04,320
So in certain directions, look at this wave from this opening.
所以从某些方向看，注意这个从开口处发出的波。

647
01:02:04,320 --> 01:02:09,820
This one here had just this one was one wavelength to here this one was two.
这个只有一个波长，这个有两个。

648
01:02:09,820 --> 01:02:10,960
This one was three.
这个是三。

649
01:02:10,960 --> 01:02:19,420
So in this particular direction, all of these waves are in phase and they contribute to positive interference.
因此，在这个特定方向上，所有这些波都同相，会产生建设性干涉。

650
01:02:19,420 --> 01:02:23,360
And that is called the Bragg condition.
这被称为布拉格条件。

651
01:02:23,360 --> 01:02:31,760
Each of these diffraction patterns I can now project here in the pupil plane for the lens as a particular spot.
我现在可以将这些衍射图样中的每一个，投影到透镜的孔径平面上，形成一个特定的光斑。

652
01:02:31,760 --> 01:02:36,960
And when these diffraction patterns start to fall outside the aperture of the lens,
当这些衍射图样开始超出透镜的孔径范围，

653
01:02:36,960 --> 01:02:45,840
the numerical aperture of the lens, then no longer does it contribute to the image formation at the wafer level.
也就是超出透镜的数值孔径时，它们就不再对晶圆层面的成像产生贡献。

654
01:02:45,840 --> 01:02:48,340
It basically looks like something like this.
它看起来大致像这样。

655
01:02:48,340 --> 01:02:49,480
My zeroth order.
我的零级衍射。

656
01:02:49,480 --> 01:02:52,880
The light that straight goes through these waves.
指的是直接穿过这些光栅的光。

657
01:02:52,880 --> 01:02:55,580
They lead to no contrast here.
它们在这里不会产生对比度。

658
01:02:55,580 --> 01:03:06,340
The first order is a wave with the same frequency as the pattern, the second order is triple the frequency, et cetera.
一级衍射是与图案频率相同的波，二级衍射是三倍频率，依此类推。

659
01:03:06,340 --> 01:03:12,540
So that's how in the end, I reconstruct the image at the wafer plane.
这就是我最终在晶圆平面上重建图像的方式。

660
01:03:12,540 --> 01:03:13,960
I'm going a little bit fast.
我讲得有点快。

661
01:03:13,960 --> 01:03:26,020
So now Abe was the one that said so now my challenge is I know what I want as a wafer,
现在，安倍说的是，我的挑战在于，我清楚自己想要的晶圆上的光强分布，

662
01:03:26,020 --> 01:03:29,460
as a light intensity on the wafer plane.
也就是晶圆平面上的光强。

663
01:03:29,460 --> 01:03:37,570
My challenge is to optimize the source here so that for every source point, the waves hitting the mask
我的挑战是优化这里的光源，使得每个光源点发出的波在经过掩模、通过透镜以及所有路径长度差异后，

664
01:03:37,570 --> 01:03:48,730
with how they go through the lens and all the path length differences, how that all adds up to this spatial frequency on the mask.
最终叠加起来，正好形成掩模上的这个空间频率。

665
01:03:48,730 --> 01:03:50,390
Let me show that to you.
让我给你们演示一下。

666
01:03:50,390 --> 01:03:51,730
Much simpler.
简单多了。

667
01:03:51,730 --> 01:04:02,830
Here we have that one central point that I was talking about this large illumination disk hitting a mask, creating diffraction patterns.
这里我们看到那个我之前提到的中心点，一个大的照明光斑照射到掩模上，产生衍射图案。

668
01:04:02,830 --> 01:04:06,930
Each of these diffraction patterns are within the pupil plane of the lens,
这些衍射图案都位于透镜的孔径平面内，

669
01:04:06,930 --> 01:04:13,210
and therefore they contribute to this interference pattern on the wafer.
因此它们共同贡献了晶圆上的这个干涉图案。

670
01:04:13,210 --> 01:04:16,510
What happens now when I start to reduce the pitch.
现在我开始减小节距时会发生什么。

671
01:04:19,050 --> 01:04:23,410
You see that some of the diffraction now moves further out.
你看到一些衍射图案现在向外移动得更远了。

672
01:04:23,410 --> 01:04:26,450
The contrast in my image starts to reduce.
我图像的对比度开始下降。

673
01:04:26,450 --> 01:04:31,870
And I'm now at a CD basically of 0.5 lambda over an A.
现在我处于一个相当于0.5倍波长除以A的CD值。

674
01:04:31,870 --> 01:04:36,710
If I now go any further with shrinking,
如果我现在继续缩小尺寸，

675
01:04:36,710 --> 01:04:44,310
suddenly those outer points no longer are captured by the lens, and I have 0 contrast left.
那些外侧的点突然就不再被镜头捕捉到，对比度完全消失。

676
01:04:44,310 --> 01:04:46,190
There's no imaging.
图像无法形成。

677
01:04:46,190 --> 01:04:46,970
But wait a minute.
但等一下。

678
01:04:46,970 --> 01:04:49,350
I can do some tricks.
我可以玩些技巧。

679
01:04:49,350 --> 01:04:54,730
What if instead of using that point source, if I use a whole disk.
如果我不使用点光源，而是用一个完整的圆盘呢？

680
01:04:57,310 --> 01:05:05,230
Now you see that right here at the edge, there is, again, a little bit of overlap between the zeroth order and the first order.
现在你看到，在边缘位置，零级和一级光之间再次出现一点重叠。

681
01:05:05,230 --> 01:05:14,070
So I start to see a little bit of the reconstruction of my image at the wafer plane.
因此，我开始在晶圆平面上看到一点图像重建。

682
01:05:14,070 --> 01:05:25,070
But the contrast is very low because there is a lot of light from the center that doesn't really contribute anything to the interference.
但对比度很低，因为中心的大量光线并未真正参与干涉。

683
01:05:25,070 --> 01:05:27,850
So what if I could move that light.
那如果我能移动这些光线呢？

684
01:05:27,850 --> 01:05:30,660
That would improve my contrast.
这样就能提升对比度。

685
01:05:30,660 --> 01:05:34,700
So I go and use what we call annular illumination.
于是我使用我们称之为环形照明的技术。

686
01:05:34,700 --> 01:05:37,880
Instead of the light coming out of that whole disk, I now see it.
不再是从整个圆盘发出的光，我现在能看到它了。

687
01:05:37,880 --> 01:05:47,100
If I look from the mask back at the illumination, I would see it come from a ring and I get much better contrast.
如果我从掩模看向照明，会发现光来自一个环形，对比度显著提高。

688
01:05:47,100 --> 01:05:50,500
Well, if I can do that, why not do even more.
既然能做到这一点，为什么不做得更进一步？

689
01:05:50,500 --> 01:05:54,660
Because that light here at the edges is also not contributing.
因为边缘的光也并未发挥作用。

690
01:05:54,660 --> 01:05:57,560
This is where the positive interference come from.
这正是正向干涉产生的地方。

691
01:05:57,560 --> 01:06:00,340
So let me remove that also.
那么让我也把这部分去掉。

692
01:06:00,340 --> 01:06:02,820
And I get even better contrast.
这样对比度进一步提升。

693
01:06:02,820 --> 01:06:06,780
Now I have something called dipole illumination.
现在我有了所谓的双极照明。

694
01:06:06,780 --> 01:06:12,740
And that is what a lot of the fancy stuff that is happening nowadays.
这正是当今许多先进光刻技术的核心。

695
01:06:12,740 --> 01:06:19,360
We can basically create with our illumination arbitrary shapes for the illumination.
我们基本上可以通过照明系统，为光刻过程创建任意形状的照明。

696
01:06:19,360 --> 01:06:25,600
And what is the best illumination that will for the set of patterns lead to the best reconstruction.
而最佳的照明方式，就是能让这一组图案实现最精确重构的照明。

697
01:06:29,480 --> 01:06:31,520
How does that then work out.
那样的话是怎么运作的呢。

698
01:06:31,520 --> 01:06:39,920
If I have a full chip design, I will pick a bunch of critical patterns, the ones that I care about most.
如果我有一个完整的芯片设计，我会挑选出一组关键图案，也就是我最关心的那些。

699
01:06:39,920 --> 01:06:42,900
For those, I will start doing this optimization.
对这些图案，我会开始进行这种优化。

700
01:06:42,900 --> 01:06:46,240
I have a forward model, I keep calculating,
我有一个前向模型，会持续进行计算。

701
01:06:46,240 --> 01:06:54,280
I can use inverse lithography and try to do a more direct calculation, but in the end, I will end up with an illumination.
我可以使用逆光刻技术，尝试进行更直接的计算，但最终还是会得到一个照明方案。

702
01:06:54,280 --> 01:06:56,400
You can see that there at the top.
你可以在上面看到这个。

703
01:06:56,400 --> 01:07:00,080
And with that illumination I can.
拥有这个照明方案后，我就可以。

704
01:07:00,080 --> 01:07:01,020
Yeah there you go.
对，就是这样。

705
01:07:01,020 --> 01:07:04,740
We start to improve, iterate on the illumination.
我们开始改进并迭代照明方案。

706
01:07:04,740 --> 01:07:10,040
And you can now start seeing that as I project I get a cleaner and cleaner image.
现在你可以看到，随着我进行投影，图像变得越来越清晰。

707
01:07:10,040 --> 01:07:18,640
Once I have the very best illumination, I can say, OK, now let me use with this illumination OPC to improve the whole mask.
一旦我得到了最佳的照明方案，我就可以说，好了，现在让我用这个照明方案配合 OPC 来优化整个掩模。

708
01:07:18,640 --> 01:07:22,940
And if I did the original selection of the patterns that I optimized for.
如果我当初选择了那些我优化过的图案。

709
01:07:22,940 --> 01:07:29,680
Well, and those were really the most critical ones then this illumination will actually work for the whole chip.
嗯，那些是最关键的，这样照明就能适用于整个芯片。

710
01:07:33,020 --> 01:07:36,940
So how does that optimization algorithm work.
那么这个优化算法是如何工作的？

711
01:07:36,940 --> 01:07:45,900
Basically we tend to look at hey, I want to this is what the designer drew this square thing.
基本上我们通常会考虑，我想实现的是设计者画出的这个方形结构。

712
01:07:45,900 --> 01:07:48,840
Now we know that we can never print something square.
现在我们知道，永远无法打印出一个真正的方形。

713
01:07:48,840 --> 01:07:51,340
There's always finite resolution.
总存在有限的分辨率。

714
01:07:51,340 --> 01:07:56,300
So if I would try to optimize directly to that square shape,
所以如果我直接优化到这个方形形状，

715
01:07:56,300 --> 01:08:02,600
my total cost function, which is all the errors added up, would be completely dominated by these corners.
我的总成本函数，也就是所有误差相加的结果，将完全被这些角落所主导。

716
01:08:02,600 --> 01:08:03,960
And that's artificial.
这是人为造成的。

717
01:08:03,960 --> 01:08:09,740
So we say, theoretically the best that I can do is some target that I can draw here.
所以我们说，理论上我能做到的最好情况是这里画出的一个目标形状。

718
01:08:09,740 --> 01:08:19,960
Let me now try to get the mask and the illumination so that I get as close as possible to what I think is possible, and I want to do that for a range of conditions,
现在我要尝试找到掩模和照明，使结果尽可能接近我认为可能实现的形状，并且要在一系列条件下实现这一点，

719
01:08:19,960 --> 01:08:25,290
not just for nominal, but also for a little bit more or less dose.
而不仅仅是标准条件，还包括剂量稍多或稍少的情况。

720
01:08:25,290 --> 01:08:27,569
Dose is never perfectly controlled.
剂量永远无法完全精确控制。

721
01:08:27,569 --> 01:08:29,850
A little bit more.
稍微多一点。

722
01:08:29,850 --> 01:08:34,109
Some focus variation and the mask making is also not perfect.
有一些焦点变化，掩模制作也不完美。

723
01:08:34,109 --> 01:08:43,569
So I take all these variances into account and make sure that I arrive at something that is robust under these variations.
因此我考虑了所有这些变化因素，确保最终结果在这些变化下依然稳健。

724
01:08:43,569 --> 01:08:46,330
Here are some of the masks that I will skip.
这里有一些我会跳过的掩模。

725
01:08:46,330 --> 01:08:51,630
Here are some of the math that I will also skip that determines how all of that works.
这里有一些我会跳过的数学计算，它们决定了整个过程的工作原理。

726
01:08:51,630 --> 01:09:02,850
But what I wanted to point out here is there are actually two terms here that is this here that captures some of the effects from non chemically amplified resist.
但我想指出的是，这里实际上有两个项，其中这一项捕捉了非化学放大光刻胶的一些效应。

727
01:09:02,850 --> 01:09:07,970
And I want right now to focus your attention here for a moment at this term.
现在我想请大家暂时关注这一项。

728
01:09:07,970 --> 01:09:10,210
This is a mask 3D effect.
这是掩模的三维效应。

729
01:09:10,210 --> 01:09:13,609
So what is a mask 3D effect.
那么什么是掩模的三维效应？

730
01:09:13,609 --> 01:09:17,450
I'll go fast I'm nearly done.
我会讲得快一些，我快讲完了。

731
01:09:17,450 --> 01:09:20,189
Here is one of those poles of the illumination.
这是照明中的一个极点。

732
01:09:20,189 --> 01:09:22,810
The zeroth order is light that goes through.
零阶是直接通过的光。

733
01:09:22,810 --> 01:09:24,910
It goes to my wafer.
它会落在我的晶圆上。

734
01:09:24,910 --> 01:09:28,870
Here is the first diffraction order and it goes here.
这是第一个衍射级次，它会到这里。

735
01:09:28,870 --> 01:09:36,109
Well, because of electromagnetic effects here, there is an extra phase difference between these two.
由于这里的电磁效应，这两者之间会产生额外的相位差。

736
01:09:36,109 --> 01:09:38,250
That's called a mask 3D effect.
这被称为掩模三维效应。

737
01:09:38,250 --> 01:09:47,130
And that means that instead of a really good reconstruction of all my Fourier components, imagine that I have a Fourier transform.
这意味着，而不是完美地重建我所有的傅里叶分量，想象一下我有一个傅里叶变换。

738
01:09:47,130 --> 01:09:57,230
But I'm a little bit off on the amplitude of some of these components, or I'm a little bit off on the phase of these components that would start to affect your reconstruction.
但这些分量中有些的振幅略有偏差，或者这些分量的相位略有偏差，这将开始影响你的重建效果。

739
01:09:57,230 --> 01:10:01,530
So our goal is to reconstruct how can I do that correctly.
因此，我们的目标是正确地重建出这种现象。

740
01:10:01,530 --> 01:10:04,910
Because my one pole remember the dipole illumination.
因为我记得，我的照明是偶极子照明。

741
01:10:04,910 --> 01:10:06,310
This was one pole.
这是一个偶极子。

742
01:10:06,310 --> 01:10:11,370
And as a result of that phase difference you actually get a shift in your mask.
由于这种相位差，实际上你的掩模会出现偏移。

743
01:10:11,370 --> 01:10:16,490
You see this phi minus phi be that phase difference leads to a shift in your mask.
你看到这个 φ 减 φ′，这个相位差导致了掩模的偏移。

744
01:10:16,490 --> 01:10:23,180
Instead of the intensity being focused around the ideal position, it has shifted a little bit.
本来强度应该集中在理想位置，但它已经发生了一点偏移。

745
01:10:23,180 --> 01:10:27,220
Now the other pole will have this shift in the other direction.
现在另一个光斑将朝相反方向发生偏移。

746
01:10:27,220 --> 01:10:34,020
So my total image is now the sum of two distributions.
因此，我的整体图像现在是两个分布的总和。

747
01:10:34,020 --> 01:10:38,640
If they were perfectly aligned I would have a nice sharp image, but they are not.
如果它们完全对齐，我将得到一个清晰锐利的图像，但它们并非如此。

748
01:10:38,640 --> 01:10:43,300
So the image fades I get a reduction in contrast.
所以图像变得模糊，对比度降低。

749
01:10:43,300 --> 01:10:44,540
What could I do.
我能做些什么呢？

750
01:10:44,540 --> 01:10:47,020
Could I do something smart.
我能不能做点聪明的事？

751
01:10:47,020 --> 01:10:56,120
What if I have the illumination and instead of the dipole here, I move this pole down a little bit.
如果我调整照明方式，不再把这种双极结构放在这里，而是把这个光斑稍微往下移一点。

752
01:10:56,120 --> 01:11:03,260
I move this pole up a little bit, and in my lens I can now compensate for the mask's 3D effects.
我把这个光斑稍微往上移一点，这样在透镜中我就能补偿掩模的三维效应。

753
01:11:03,260 --> 01:11:12,680
Because this order here, these diffraction orders here and here are the zeroth order.
因为这里的这些衍射级次，也就是这里的零级衍射。

754
01:11:12,680 --> 01:11:19,720
And now I can have the one pole shift to the left, the other one a little bit to the right.
现在我可以让一个光斑向左移动，另一个稍微向右移动。

755
01:11:19,720 --> 01:11:22,880
And now they overlap again perfectly.
这样它们又能完美重叠了。

756
01:11:22,880 --> 01:11:24,560
Now that's simple.
现在这就简单了。

757
01:11:24,560 --> 01:11:29,140
If I only have to do with a 2D pattern, what we can now do.
如果我只需要处理一个二维图案，我们现在能做到的事情。

758
01:11:29,140 --> 01:11:33,340
And that's why we have computers, I can actually generalize this.
这就是为什么我们需要计算机，我实际上可以将这一方法泛化。

759
01:11:33,340 --> 01:11:36,720
And I can take an arbitrary mask pattern for logic.
我可以为逻辑电路任意设定一个掩模图案。

760
01:11:36,720 --> 01:11:48,920
And I can say, hey, what would now be the very best aberration pattern in my lens that would make that all these images from these poles overlap as well as possible.
我可以问，现在我的镜头中什么样的像差模式能最好地使这些来自不同光路的图像尽可能重合。

761
01:11:48,920 --> 01:11:50,800
And that's what you see here.
这就是你们在这里看到的。

762
01:11:50,800 --> 01:11:58,240
Here is what I just explained for a simple if all I look at is lens is lines and spaces.
这是我刚才用一个简单情况说明的，即我只关注镜头中的线条和间距。

763
01:11:58,240 --> 01:12:02,720
This is for the actual mask pattern here.
这是针对这里实际掩模图案的情况。

764
01:12:02,720 --> 01:12:10,080
And as a result, I get much better exposure, latitude and much better adaptive focus in my final imaging.
因此，我最终获得的曝光宽容度更高，焦点适应性也显著提升。

765
01:12:10,080 --> 01:12:18,680
So I hope that with that, I've given you a little bit of a flavor on how we can use computation to optimize the settings on the scanner,
所以我希望通过这些内容，能让你们对如何利用计算优化光刻机的设置有了一点直观感受。

766
01:12:18,680 --> 01:12:23,140
both from an illumination perspective as well as aberrations in the lens.
无论是从照明角度，还是镜头像差方面。

767
01:12:23,140 --> 01:12:31,340
We try to minimize the aberrations, and sometimes we introduce them on purpose to correct for mass 3D effects.
我们通常尽量减少像差，但有时也会故意引入像差，以补偿掩模的三维效应。

768
01:12:31,340 --> 01:12:35,060
Now, with all of that said, let me finish up the last part.
话虽如此，让我来结束最后一部分。

769
01:12:35,060 --> 01:12:39,420
Just a slide on the roadmap and the outlook.
仅简单介绍一下路线图和展望。

770
01:12:39,420 --> 01:12:45,060
Remember the best possible resolution at the lowest possible price.
记住，要在尽可能低的价格下实现最佳分辨率。

771
01:12:45,060 --> 01:12:50,200
So let's look at we've looked at the best possible resolution.
那么我们来看一下，我们已经实现了最佳可能的分辨率。

772
01:12:50,200 --> 01:12:55,540
Reduced the lambda, increase DNA decrease K1.
降低λ值，提升DNA，降低K1。

773
01:12:55,540 --> 01:13:04,380
Let's now look for a moment that cost of the technology the productivity the EUV light source.
现在我们来看一下这项技术的成本、生产效率以及EUV光源。

774
01:13:04,380 --> 01:13:13,680
We now we've recently announced that our latest results in San Diego, we can get one kilowatt of power out of our dose.
我们最近在圣地亚哥宣布了最新成果，我们已能从剂量中获得一千瓦的功率。

775
01:13:13,680 --> 01:13:19,970
And remember what Tony said in the beginning we struggled to get one Watt.
记住托尼一开始说的，我们曾为获得一瓦功率而挣扎。

776
01:13:19,970 --> 01:13:24,170
Then at some point we were really excited that we got 10 watts.
后来我们曾非常兴奋，终于达到了十瓦。

777
01:13:24,170 --> 01:13:29,990
TSMC told us that when we hit 80w, we can go into volume production.
台积电告诉我们，当达到80瓦时，我们就可以进入量产。

778
01:13:29,990 --> 01:13:32,690
That was in 2019.
那是在2019年。

779
01:13:32,690 --> 01:13:38,470
That was 2 watts or that was 281 was 2014 was 214.
那是2瓦，或者说是2014年的281瓦，2014年是214瓦。

780
01:13:38,470 --> 01:13:39,430
OK yeah.
好的，没错。

781
01:13:39,430 --> 01:13:44,310
Sorry so that's when they said, OK, now we are serious about it.
对不起，所以他们说，好吧，现在我们认真对待这件事了。

782
01:13:44,310 --> 01:13:46,090
We think that you can get there.
我们认为你们能做到这一点。

783
01:13:46,090 --> 01:13:49,970
And by 2019 we were at 250.
到2019年，我们已经达到了250。

784
01:13:49,970 --> 01:13:57,610
We now have in our hands demonstrations that we can actually hit 1 kilowatt.
现在我们手头已经有演示，证明我们实际上可以达到1千瓦。

785
01:13:57,610 --> 01:14:05,090
Another way of reducing the cost of the system is by having more commonality between EUV.
降低系统成本的另一种方式是提高EUV之间的通用性。

786
01:14:05,090 --> 01:14:11,690
Sorry, between the .33 and a system and the .55 and a system.
对不起，是指.33与系统之间，以及.55与系统之间的通用性。

787
01:14:11,690 --> 01:14:22,610
So we have a roadmap on how we can create a more common platform that we will do that with also an option to in the future,
因此我们有一条路线图，说明如何创建一个更通用的平台，我们也将为此提供未来选项，

788
01:14:22,610 --> 01:14:31,950
start looking at 0.75, for which we already have some prototype designs and where we can get at the end.
开始考虑0.75，我们已经有一些原型设计，最终可以实现这一点。

789
01:14:31,950 --> 01:14:43,610
Or here is an example of with 13.5 nanometer EUV light from Paul scherrer Institute interferometric EUV lithography, where you do not have mass 3D effects.
这里是一个例子，来自保罗·谢勒研究所的13.5纳米EUV光的干涉式EUV光刻，其中没有大规模3D效应。

790
01:14:43,610 --> 01:14:48,030
If we could really control everything can see that.
如果我们真的能控制一切，就能看到这一点。

791
01:14:48,030 --> 01:14:57,590
Yeah, there are already some evidence that half pitches of about five or six nanometer as a absolute theoretical maximum would be possible.
是的，已经有了一些证据表明，五或六纳米左右的半间距，作为绝对理论极限是可能的。

792
01:14:57,590 --> 01:15:04,670
So we still have quite a ways to go that we can scale more than where we are today.
所以我们还有很长的路要走，才能实现比今天更大的扩展。

793
01:15:04,670 --> 01:15:10,290
And with that, I come to the end, and I hope that I fulfilled my promise that I wouldn't be too long.
话说到这儿，我就讲完了，希望我没有违背承诺，讲得太长。

794
01:15:13,470 --> 01:15:15,720
Tony, why don't you join me for questions.
托尼，你为什么不和我一起回答问题呢？

795
01:15:18,700 --> 01:15:21,220
Hello what happened here.
你好，这里发生了什么？

796
01:15:21,220 --> 01:15:22,220
No it's fine.
没关系的。

797
01:15:22,220 --> 01:15:25,540
He was supposed to activate from that.
他本该从那个地方启动的。

798
01:15:25,540 --> 01:15:26,420
All right.
好的。

799
01:15:26,420 --> 01:15:27,620
Oh, I think it's on now.
噢，我觉得现在打开了。

800
01:15:27,620 --> 01:15:34,440
OK, so we'll take questions now for both speakers, and we're open for questions.
好，现在我们将为两位演讲者回答问题，欢迎大家提问。

801
01:15:38,540 --> 01:15:42,800
Do I understand correctly that if the end user cares about,
我理解得对吗，如果终端用户只关心某一轴向的分辨率，

802
01:15:42,800 --> 01:15:48,432
let's say, resolution just along one axis, that's an easier problem from your perspective.
从你们的角度来看，这个问题会更容易解决。

803
01:15:48,432 --> 01:15:54,840
Is that correct to say, is that something that the end users are trying to or you all collectively are trying to leverage.
说得对吗？这是终端用户在尝试的，还是你们大家共同在尝试利用的？

804
01:15:54,840 --> 01:15:58,180
OK, so let's define first what the end user is, right.
好，那我们先来定义一下什么是终端用户，对吧。

805
01:15:58,180 --> 01:16:08,140
If the end user is Apple then they tell TSMC it's your problem.
如果最终用户是苹果公司，他们就会告诉台积电，这是你们的问题。

806
01:16:08,140 --> 01:16:17,920
TSMC will tell us, hey, do you we want to use dipole illumination combination, because that gives the very best contrast for one dimensional patterns.
台积电会告诉我们，嘿，我们是否要使用偶极照明组合，因为这对一维图案能提供最佳对比度。

807
01:16:17,920 --> 01:16:25,360
Can you make a light source where all of the light only comes from these two points in that whole disk.
你能制造一种光源，让整个圆盘中只有这两个点发出光线吗？

808
01:16:25,360 --> 01:16:35,920
Well, we can do that pretty well, but if you make these spots too small, we can only do that by throwing some of the light away.
我们能做到相当不错，但如果把这两个光点做得太小，就只能通过舍弃部分光线来实现。

809
01:16:35,920 --> 01:16:40,520
And if we throw some of the light away, then it goes at the expense of productivity.
而如果我们舍弃部分光线，就会牺牲生产效率。

810
01:16:40,520 --> 01:16:48,900
And so our newer illumination designs can use a much smaller, what we call a pupil fill ratio.
因此，我们新的照明设计可以使用更小的、我们称之为瞳孔填充率的数值。

811
01:16:48,900 --> 01:16:54,700
What's the smallest fraction of that whole illumination disk that you can define.
你能定义的整个照明圆盘中最小的光强比例是多少？

812
01:16:54,700 --> 01:17:00,040
That's where I want the light to come from and still use 100% of the light.
我希望光线从这里发出，同时还能100%利用所有光线。

813
01:17:00,040 --> 01:17:06,440
So it's really a shared responsibility between us and the customer.
所以这实际上是英伟达和客户之间的共同责任。

814
01:17:06,440 --> 01:17:13,550
But for every layer metal 0, metal one, metal 2 contact holes, vias.
但每一层，包括金属层0、金属层1、金属层2、接触孔和通孔。

815
01:17:13,550 --> 01:17:16,590
Every layer has its own illumination.
每一层都有其独立的照明方案。

816
01:17:16,590 --> 01:17:20,150
And let me take your example a little bit to an extreme.
让我稍微把你的例子推向一个极端。

817
01:17:20,150 --> 01:17:26,830
If I want the absolute smallest pitch in one direction,
如果我想在某一方向上实现最小的间距，

818
01:17:26,830 --> 01:17:33,830
I would use a dipole with only two tiny little pieces of light here.
我会使用一个仅包含两个微小光点的偶极子。

819
01:17:33,830 --> 01:17:41,170
I would now have great contrast in this direction and 0 contrast in the other direction.
这样我就能在这个方向上获得很高的对比度，而在另一个方向上对比度为零。

820
01:17:41,170 --> 01:17:45,950
So the only thing that I can now do is print lines that are infinitely long.
因此我现在唯一能做的就是打印无限长的线条。

821
01:17:45,950 --> 01:17:49,030
Not a single designer is interested in that.
没有任何一位设计师会对这种结果感兴趣。

822
01:17:49,030 --> 01:17:55,590
So now what you could do is well, but if I have those very long lines, I will use a second exposure to cut them.
所以现在你可以这么做：如果我有这些非常长的线条，我可以用第二次曝光来切割它们。

823
01:17:55,590 --> 01:17:57,010
But that's expensive.
但这成本很高。

824
01:17:57,010 --> 01:18:01,330
Perhaps bring in these poles a little bit, regain a little bit of that contrast.
或许可以稍微调整一下这些极点的位置，重新获得一些对比度。

825
01:18:01,330 --> 01:18:06,350
And now I can also print gaps in these lines.
这样我就能在这些线条中打印出间隔。

826
01:18:06,350 --> 01:18:08,850
But how small I can get that gap.
但这个间隔最小能到多小？

827
01:18:08,850 --> 01:18:17,290
That's the so-called tip to tip difference that depends on how you optimize the illumination and how you optimize the OPC.
这就是所谓的尖端到尖端间距，它取决于照明优化和 OPC 优化的方式。

828
01:18:17,290 --> 01:18:21,850
So it's a very interactive discussion between us and our customers.
所以这是我们与客户之间非常互动的讨论。

829
01:18:21,850 --> 01:18:23,470
Hope that answers your question.
希望这能回答你的问题。

830
01:18:23,470 --> 01:18:24,830
OK, here's another question.
好的，这是另一个问题。

831
01:18:24,830 --> 01:18:26,350
Just a quick question.
只提个快速问题。

832
01:18:26,350 --> 01:18:40,310
So if the minimum pitch you're expecting is like 90 nanometers, that does bring up the question, what exactly does the metric in like a node name refer to.
所以如果你期望的最小线距大约是90纳米，这就引出了一个问题，即节点名称中的指标具体指的是什么。

833
01:18:40,310 --> 01:18:44,730
Because it's clearly not the pitch of the features themselves.
因为显然它并不是特征本身的线距。

834
01:18:44,730 --> 01:18:45,870
Great question.
很好的问题。

835
01:18:45,870 --> 01:18:52,610
Yeah so the node names right 5 nanometer node, 4 nanometer node three nanometer node.
是的，节点名称如5纳米节点、4纳米节点、3纳米节点。

836
01:18:52,610 --> 01:19:00,570
Back in the days that we had the 45 nanometer node that actually really represented the size of the lines.
以前我们有45纳米节点时，那确实代表了线条的实际尺寸。

837
01:19:00,570 --> 01:19:04,770
And at some point that became very increasingly difficult.
但后来这变得越来越困难。

838
01:19:04,770 --> 01:19:16,870
But people also became very creative in terms of with design tricks and layout tricks, I can get more density out of the size that I have.
不过人们在设计技巧和版图技巧方面也变得非常有创意，我可以用现有的尺寸实现更高的密度。

839
01:19:16,870 --> 01:19:26,770
So think of the 5 nanometer and the 4 nanometer and 3 nanometer now more as an indication of what is the effective transistor density.
所以现在可以把5纳米、4纳米和3纳米更多地看作是有效晶体管密度的指示。

840
01:19:26,770 --> 01:19:32,670
How many transistors can I get per squared per square millimeter or per square micron.
即每平方毫米或每平方微米能容纳多少个晶体管。

841
01:19:32,670 --> 01:19:37,450
It's more an indication of that instead of really the dimension.
这更多是表明这一点，而不是真正的尺寸。

842
01:19:37,450 --> 01:19:39,050
Tony, anything you would like to add.
安东尼，你还有什么想补充的吗？

843
01:19:39,050 --> 01:19:46,430
Yeah well, historically Ronald was right down to maybe 90 or 65 nanometers.
是的，从历史上看，罗纳德在90纳米或65纳米左右是正确的。

844
01:19:46,430 --> 01:19:47,890
That's the half pitch.
这是半间距。

845
01:19:47,890 --> 01:19:51,230
When you say 65, the half pitch is 65.
当你说65纳米时，半间距就是65纳米。

846
01:19:51,230 --> 01:19:56,110
But nowadays, no, it's just a marketing name.
但如今，不，这只是一个营销名称。

847
01:19:56,110 --> 01:19:57,490
But this is not recorded.
但这段内容没有被记录下来。

848
01:19:57,490 --> 01:20:00,350
I don't want my customers to hear this.
我不希望我的客户听到这些。

849
01:20:00,350 --> 01:20:01,310
They know.
他们知道。

850
01:20:01,310 --> 01:20:05,830
Yeah, it's so cut this part out of the recording, OK.
是的，把这段从录音中剪掉，好吗？

851
01:20:05,830 --> 01:20:09,520
No, it is an improvement over the previous generation.
不，这确实比前一代有所改进。

852
01:20:09,520 --> 01:20:14,080
But is it 2x the transistor density.
但它的晶体管密度是前一代的2倍吗？

853
01:20:14,080 --> 01:20:16,540
No, those days are over.
不，那些日子已经过去了。

854
01:20:16,540 --> 01:20:22,220
OK, so I'd like to ask a question about the optimization methods.
好的，我想问一下关于优化方法的问题。

855
01:20:22,220 --> 01:20:30,860
So one of the great challenges in optimization is if you have a great many variables to optimize, it gets really quite hard.
优化中的一个重大挑战是，如果你需要优化的变量非常多，就会变得非常困难。

856
01:20:30,860 --> 01:20:36,540
Now you spoke mostly about the source optimization.
你现在主要讲的是光源优化。

857
01:20:36,540 --> 01:20:39,980
And there's a lot of variables in the source optimization.
光源优化中有很多变量。

858
01:20:39,980 --> 01:20:45,500
But then you also mention the so-called OPC which is the mask optimization.
但你同时也提到了所谓的 OPC，也就是掩模优化。

859
01:20:45,500 --> 01:20:52,780
And that adds even more variables because in principle the geometric shapes can be represented by an infinite number of variables.
这会带来更多的变量，因为理论上几何形状可以用无限多个变量来表示。

860
01:20:52,780 --> 01:20:55,260
So you have a very huge number of variables.
所以你面对的是一个极其庞大的变量数量。

861
01:20:55,260 --> 01:21:01,878
So shouldn't you be doing the optimization of all of them together rather than saying, I'm going to do source optimization.
那你为什么不同时优化所有变量，而是说我要先做光源优化？

862
01:21:01,878 --> 01:21:07,500
You should be saying, I'm going to do the optimization of everything the source, the mask.
你应该说，我要一次性优化所有内容，包括光源和掩模。

863
01:21:07,500 --> 01:21:09,500
I do it all in one big optimization.
我把所有内容放在一个大的优化过程中完成。

864
01:21:09,500 --> 01:21:12,820
Yeah so let me first answer that question.
好的，让我先回答这个问题。

865
01:21:12,820 --> 01:21:13,900
You're absolutely right.
你说得完全正确。

866
01:21:13,900 --> 01:21:16,280
And perhaps I wasn't completely clear.
或许我之前表达得还不够清楚。

867
01:21:16,280 --> 01:21:22,060
Remember that video where we picked some clips out of this huge design.
记得我们从这个巨大设计中挑选了一些片段的那段视频吗？

868
01:21:22,060 --> 01:21:33,240
Those clips were supposed to be representative proxies for the incredible variety of patterns of the whole design.
这些片段本应作为整个设计中惊人多样图案的代表性代理。

869
01:21:33,240 --> 01:21:40,280
When we optimize the illumination, we optimize that with the OPC for those clips.
当我们优化照明时，是针对这些片段的 OPC 进行优化的。

870
01:21:40,280 --> 01:21:49,480
And then we but we cannot say, let's optimize the whole design with hundreds of billions of patterns,
但我们不能说，让我们用数百亿个图案，

871
01:21:49,480 --> 01:21:56,040
together with all these variables in the illumination and with all of the variables in the projection optics.
以及照明中的所有变量和投影光学中的所有变量，一起优化整个设计。

872
01:21:56,040 --> 01:21:59,560
That's simply computationally is not yet feasible.
这在计算上目前还不可行。

873
01:21:59,560 --> 01:22:02,080
So what we do is we take some of these clips.
所以我们做的，是选取其中一些片段。

874
01:22:02,080 --> 01:22:02,900
There we go.
就是这样。

875
01:22:02,900 --> 01:22:12,130
Optimize then we say, now this illumination, probably since it is good for the most critical patterns, will be good for all of the other patterns.
优化之后，我们说，既然这种照明对最关键的图案有效，那它很可能对其他所有图案也有效。

876
01:22:12,130 --> 01:22:15,450
And then we do the OPC, a divide and conquer strategy.
然后我们再进行 OPC，采用分而治之的策略。

877
01:22:15,450 --> 01:22:19,330
Once the OPC stage, you don't change the design anymore.
OPC 阶段之后，你就不能再修改设计了。

878
01:22:19,330 --> 01:22:23,970
I'm going to have to cut us off our no, no I'm sorry.
我得打断一下，抱歉，不行。

879
01:22:23,970 --> 01:22:29,210
Our AV support is going to leave us and we're well after time.
我们的自动驾驶支持团队要离开了，而且已经超时了。

880
01:22:29,210 --> 01:22:36,070
But the speakers will stick around and happy to answer questions one on one.
但演讲者会留下来，很乐意一对一回答问题。

881
01:22:36,070 --> 01:22:40,210
So let's thank both speakers for a fascinating talk.
那么，让我们感谢两位演讲者带来了一场精彩的分享。

882
01:22:44,270 --> 01:22:49,370
And if you want to stick around, I think they'll be glad to answer for the questions.
如果你想留下来，我觉得他们很乐意继续回答问题。

883
01:22:49,370 --> 01:22:53,190
Absolutely, absolutely.
当然，当然。

884
01:22:53,190 --> 01:22:54,710
How are you.
你好啊。

885
01:22:54,710 --> 01:22:57,090
Oh, I haven't seen you for a long time.
哦，好久没见你了。

886
01:22:57,090 --> 01:22:59,410
Yeah so I'm doing fine.
是的，我一切都好。

887
01:22:59,410 --> 01:23:03,250
And I understand that you are retired or not yet.
我听说你已经退休了，还是还没退休？

888
01:23:03,250 --> 01:23:04,810
Yes, I am semi-retired.
是的，我半退休了。

889
01:23:04,810 --> 01:23:06,060
I'm
我
